"TGA extends road transport compliance deadline to February 2027 - Latest News from Saudi Arabia and the World (https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/664493/saudi-arabia/saudi-arabia-extends-road-transport-compliance-deadline-to-february-2027)\nciteturn9search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: yesterday; # TGA extends road transport compliance deadline to February 2027 ... RIYADH — Saudi Arabia has extended several regulatory compliance deadlines for road transport companies operating in freight and private passenger bus services until Feb. 27, 2027, giving businesses additional time to meet requirements under the Kingdom’s Land Transport Law.\n\n# TGA extends road transport compliance deadline to February 2027\n\nSeptember 11, 2026 | 09:06 PM\n\nSeptember 11, 2026 | 09:06 PM\n\nSaudi Gazette\n\nLast Updated: September 11, 2026 | 09:06 PM\n\nImage\n\n3 minute read\n\nA A\n\nResize\n\nImage: increase-icon\n\nRIYADH — Saudi Arabia has extended several regulatory compliance deadlines for road transport companies operating in freight and private passenger bus services until Feb. 27, 2027, giving businesses additional time to meet requirements under the Kingdom’s Land Transport Law.\n\nMinister of Transport and Logistic Services and Chairman of the Transport General Authority Saleh Al-Jasser issued two decisions covering commercial and non-commercial heavy and light freight transport as well as private passenger transport by bus.\n\nThe first decision extends the deadline for private passenger bus operators to add newly introduced activity classifications to their commercial registrations, a requirement for obtaining operating licenses.\n\nIt also gives operators additional time to align their operations with regulatory requirements under the Land Transport Law and its implementing regulations.\n\nThe second decision extends deadlines for commercial and non-commercial heavy freight operators to meet several requirements, including changing vehicle registration classifications from “private transport” to “public transport” and obtaining vehicle operating cards.\n\nCommercial and non-commercial light freight operators were also granted additional time to obtain professional driver cards and bring their operations into compliance with the regulations governing the activity.\n\nThe Transport General Authority said the extensions would give affected businesses additional time to complete regulatory procedures, improve compliance and ensure the continuity of their operations within the approved legal framework.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSaudi Arabia to develop over 14 GW of computing capacity to accelerate AI growth - Latest News from Saudi Arabia and the World (https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/664498/saudi-arabia/saudi-arabia-developing-over-14-gw-of-computing-capacity-to-accelerate-ai-growth)\nciteturn9search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: today; # Saudi Arabia to develop over 14 GW of computing capacity to accelerate AI growthSeptember 12, 2026 | 06:49 AM\n\n# Saudi Arabia to develop over 14 GW of computing capacity to accelerate AI growth\n\nSeptember 12, 2026 | 06:49 AM\n\nMinister of Communications and Information Technology Abdullah Al-Swaha discusses in Silicon Valley with OpenAI CEO Sam Altman expanding collaboration in advanced AI models.\n\nSeptember 12, 2026 | 06:49 AM\n\nSaudi Gazette\n\nLast Updated: September 12, 2026 | 06:49 AM\n\nImage\n\n3 minute read\n\nA A\n\nResize\n\nImage: increase-icon\n\nSILICON VALLEY — Saudi Arabia is working with the private sector to develop more than 14 gigawatts of computing capacity as it builds an integrated model to attract artificial intelligence companies and accelerate their growth, Minister of Communications and Information Technology Abdullah Al-Swaha said.\n\nSpeaking at the opening of the fourth Frontier Leaders Forum 2026 in Silicon Valley, California, Al-Swaha said the Kingdom’s approach centers on providing AI companies with three critical components: computing capacity, capital and access to customers.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSaudi TGA extends road transport compliance deadline to Feb 2027 (https://www.gccbusinessnews.com/saudi-tga-extend-road-transport-compliance/)\nciteturn9search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: yesterday; Home Industry Transport Saudi TGA extends road transport compliance deadline to Feb 2027 ...   *   *   * Saudi Arabia’s Transport General Authority (TGA) has extended the regulatory compliance deadline for road transport establishments until February 27, 2027, covering operators in heavy and light goods transport and private bus passenger transport.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTGA extends road transport compliance deadline to February 2027 - Gulfdays. (https://gulfdays.net/tga-extends-road-transport-compliance-deadline-to-february-2027/)\nciteturn9search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: today; # TGA extends road transport compliance deadline to February 2027 ... RIYADH — Saudi Arabia has extended several regulatory compliance deadlines for road transport companies operating in freight and private passenger bus services until Feb. 27, 2027, giving businesses additional time to meet requirements under the Kingdom’s Land Transport Law.Minister of Transport and Logistic Services and Chairman of the Transport General Authority Saleh Al-Jasser issued two decisions covering commercial and non-commercial heavy and light freight transport as well as private passenger transport by bus.The first decision extends the deadline for private passenger bus operators to add newly introduced activity classifications to their commercial registrations, a requirement for obtaining operating licenses.It also gives operators additional time to align their operations with regulatory requirements under 